course: dictionary
lesson: 9473
title: Stationary or stationery?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stationary means not moving. A stationary object is standing still. «The bus was stationary at the traffic lights» tells you it had stopped and was not going anywhere. Check the clues around the word: if the sentence describes something standing still, you need stationary.
explain: Stationary can also mean not changing. «The number of pupils stayed stationary all year» tells you the number did not go up or down. So the word can be about staying the same, not only about not moving.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Never walk behind a stationary bus» is a road safety rule: a bus that is standing still may suddenly move, so keep your distance. A stationary bike is one that stays in one place, like an exercise bike in a gym.
fact: Stationary means not moving, standing still.
fact: Stationary can also mean not changing: «the number stayed stationary».
fact: Stationery, with an e, means paper, pens and envelopes. Stationary, with an a, means standing still.
fact: In science, a stationary object has a speed of zero.
fact: Phrases you will meet include remain stationary, stationary vehicle and stationary bike.
exercise: «The stationary car sat at the red light.» What does stationary mean? | *Standing still, not moving | Shiny and new | Moving very fast | Being painted
exercise: Which word means paper, pens and envelopes? | *stationery | stationary | statue | station
exercise: «The number of pupils stayed stationary all term.» What does stationary suggest? | It moved to a new school | *It did not change | It went down quickly | It went up every week
test: «Never walk behind a stationary bus, because it may move.» Why is this a safety rule? | Stationary means the bus is broken | Buses are always fast | Buses are painted in bright colours | *A bus that is standing still may suddenly move
test: On a distance–time graph, what does a flat line show? | *An object that is stationary | A fast car | A bus driving uphill | A stationery shop
exam: Which sentence uses stationary correctly? | The shop sold stationary, pens and envelopes | *The stationary bike stayed in the gym all day | Stationary is a word for letters and paper | The stationary car sped past the school
